{
  "_comment": [
    "The canonical Delicia catalogue — the reference for what a COMPLETE",
    "product row looks like.",
    "",
    "This file is the tracked replacement for the old `scripts/*.py` seed and",
    "migration scripts, which were removed in October 2026. It is the single",
    "source of truth for:",
    "",
    "  * the demo catalogue (27 products, 7 categories) the app seeds with;",
    "  * the size-option labels and their price multipliers;",
    "",
    "WHY A JSON REFERENCE EXISTS",
    "",
    "In October 2026 the catalogue was wiped. A `PATCH` against the Realtime",
    "Database REST API replaces every child node it touches *wholesale*",
    "instead of merging into them, so a partial body silently DELETES every",
    "field it does not mention. The rows came back with nothing but the",
    "translated fields, `Productsdb.fromMap` fell back to `price = 0.0`, and",
    "every price in the app rendered as \"0 ₫\".",
    "",
    "The rule that prevents a repeat: a product document is written WHOLE.",
    "Never write a partial product — always read the live row, merge, and",
    "write the complete document back.",
    "",
    "`test/catalog_integrity_test.dart` locks this contract down: every",
    "product here must declare every field the app reads, carry a price, keep",
    "its English name for search, and point at a known category."
  ],
